[
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm playing around with a \"fully computable\" version of <code>PMF</code>. A minimal example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ring</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Star</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Analysis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Normed</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Lemmas</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Rat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Star</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProbDist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The probability mass function -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pmf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- Probabilities are nonnegative -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nonneg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pmf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- Probabilities sum to 1 -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">sum_one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pmf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProbDist</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uniform</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProbDist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pmf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nonneg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">sum_one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProbDist</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uniform</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">pmf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 1 / 3</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Since <code>PMF</code> is a monad, <code>ProbDist</code> also \"morally feels like\" a monad. However, due to instances in the type signature, one cannot even write <code>Monad ProbDist</code>. Making the instances into structure fields does not help since, e.g., the definition of <code>pure : {α} → α → ProbDist α</code> would still need those instances, which means <code>pure</code> cannot be given to <code>Monad</code>.</p>\n<p>The only thing I can think of would be to \"reinvent\" <code>Monad</code> in that setting (something like <code>class MonadOnDecidableFintypes</code>) and then I'm not sure how much additional work would be needed to get e.g. <code>do</code>-notation... This feels like I'm doing something stupid.</p>\n<p>Is there some reasonable way to make this work?</p>",
        "id": 585083674,
        "sender_full_name": "Adomas Baliuka",
        "timestamp": 1776041114
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a specific reason you have decided to choose pmf output be in the rationals ( or just due to computational concerns) ? And i guess this would be specific to finite outcomes, there are PMFs over countable spaces like Poisson distribution has a PMF over naturals. That would also be an example of a PMF that specifically uses irrational values.</p>",
        "id": 585086835,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1776043810
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I want to do <code>#eval</code> and I don't need countable spaces, only finite, that's why I put in a \"non-removable\" <code>Fintype</code> instance. </p>\n<p>Actually, I'm not sure yet if I'm <em>really</em> going to use this for anything, this is just playing around. All the more reason I very much appreciate any views on what I'm doing, even though my question strictly speaking has nothing to do with probabilities and rather only with functional programming. That's why I included the example.</p>",
        "id": 585087159,
        "sender_full_name": "Adomas Baliuka",
        "timestamp": 1776044090
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This has been discussed before in the context of <code>Monad Finset</code> and also regarding universe polymorphism in monads</p>",
        "id": 585087252,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776044182
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Fixing this would require moving the type quantification out of the monad typeclass fields and into the type itself, which would then require modifying the implementation of do notation</p>",
        "id": 585087400,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776044307
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm on mobile so can't easily do so, but I'd recommend trying to find past threads on this</p>",
        "id": 585087427,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776044338
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I found an instance <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Data/Finset/Functor.html#Finset.functor\">Finset.functor</a>, whose docstring says that </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Because <code>Finset.image</code> requires a <code>DecidableEq</code> instance for the target type, we can only construct <code>Functor Finset</code>when working classically.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I guess this might be relevant: <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113488\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Changing.20the.20functor.20typeclasses/with/538553155\">#general &gt; Changing the functor typeclasses</a> </p>\n<p>Were you referring to these <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"310045\">@Eric Wieser</span> ? I also find that <del>there doesn't seem to be a <code>Monad Finset</code> instance right now</del> (though there used to be one according to  <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/How.20to.20prove.20that.20.E2.8A.82.20list.20mapping.20.20results.20in.20.E2.8A.82.20btwn.20lists/near/544850980\">#new members &gt; How to prove that ⊂ list mapping  results in ⊂ btwn lists @ 💬</a> ?!).</p>",
        "id": 585230738,
        "sender_full_name": "Adomas Baliuka",
        "timestamp": 1776096944
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"638715\">Adomas Baliuka</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Monad.20conditional.20on.20instances.3F/near/585230738\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I also find that there doesn't seem to be a <code>Monad Finset</code> instance right now</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.instMonad#doc\">docs#Finset.instMonad</a></p>",
        "id": 585239945,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776099520
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So this means that I could either use <code>Classical</code> (would prevent me from using <code>#eval</code>) or some very-complicated-sounding modification of <code>do</code>-notation. I guess I'll have to give up on making my <code>ProbDist</code> into a monad.</p>\n<p>Thanks for the help!</p>",
